---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import DetailCard from '../components/DetailCard.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Experience"
  description="Internships and roles — treasury data tooling at Cisco, webmaster for Purdue Crew."
>
  <h1>Experience</h1>
  <p>Most recent first.</p>

  <DetailCard
    title="Treasury Intern · Cisco"
    meta="June – August 2026 · New York, NY (hybrid)"
    summary="Built the treasury team's data tooling — risk models, bank analytics, and an AI workflow for broker analysis."
    open
  >
    <p>
      Cisco's treasury team manages the company's cash, investments, and share buybacks. Over the
      summer I built out the team's data tooling in Python (pandas, NumPy), shipped as a
      command-line tool the whole team uses:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Bank revenue dashboard</strong> (Excel) — evaluates roughly twenty counterparty
        banks on our trades and their long-run markups.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Value-at-Risk model</strong> — moved the team's risk forecasting from historical
        volatility to implied volatility, making the estimates forward-looking instead of
        backward-looking.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Transaction classifier</strong> — K-Means clustering distilled into a
        decision-tree surrogate, so every classification stays explainable. It categorized
        100,000+ transactions and identified miscategorized transactions that the cash team
        confirmed and reclassified.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Agentic AI workflow</strong> — turns a static buyback sheet into full broker
        analysis automatically.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </DetailCard>

  <DetailCard
    title="Webmaster · Purdue Crew"
    meta="March 2026 – present · West Lafayette, IN"
    summary="I run the rowing team's website and am building its athlete portal."
  >
    <p>
      I design and maintain <a href="https://purduecrew.com">purduecrew.com</a>, the website for
      Purdue's rowing team, and I'm building a portal where athletes, coaches, and parents can
      interact with a database of athlete metrics, race schedules, and workout plans.
    </p>
  </DetailCard>
</BaseLayout>
